.TH BERYLLIUM-CHROOT 1 "Jul 2026" "Beryllium Tools" "Beryllium System Administration"
.SH NAME
beryl-chroot \- chroot into a Beryllium OS installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B beryl-chroot
\fIBTRFS_PARTITION\fR \fIBOOT_PARTITION\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B beryl-chroot
is a utility that simplifies chrooting into a Beryllium OS installation by
automatically mounting the Btrfs subvolumes and boot partition. It is
primarily used for system repairs, updates, or maintenance of an existing
Beryllium OS installation from a live environment.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.BR BTRFS_PARTITION
The Btrfs partition containing the Beryllium OS system (e.g., /dev/sda3)
.TP
.BR BOOT_PARTITION
The boot partition containing the EFI files (e.g., /dev/sda2)
.SH OPERATION
The tool performs the following operations:
.PP
.RS 4
1. Mounts the specified Btrfs partition with standard Beryllium OS subvolumes (@, @home, @log, @pkg)
.br
2. Mounts the boot partition
.br
3. Chroots into the system
.br
4. After exiting the chroot, automatically unmounts everything
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B beryl-chroot /dev/sdb3 /dev/sdb2
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR arch-chroot (8),
.BR mount (8)
